ound the repository.\\n 2. Create a Scala file (e.g., HelloWorld.scala) in an appropriate location (maybe root or src/main/scala?).\\n    Since the issue doesn't specify a directory, we can put it in the root for simplicity.\\n 3. Write the Hello World program with comments and instructions.\\n 4. Create the GitHub Actions workflow in `ci/test-hello-world.yml` as specified.\\n\\n Let's start by exploring the repository.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]},{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"call-43fe94d0-073e-4160-813b-bfd7ed2c70fc\",\"content\":\"total 24\\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 box  box  4096 Oct 17 09:20 .\\ndrwxrwxrwt 1 root root 4096 Oct 17 09:21 ..\\ndrwxr-xr-x 8 box  box  4096 Oct 17 09:21 .git\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 box  box   174 Oct 17 09:20 .gitkeep\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 box  box   382 Oct 17 09:20 README.md\\n\",\"name\":\"bash\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":null,\"tool_calls\":[{\"id\":\"call-12a9f39c-e680-4d90-bb32-ae6d07646cf6\",\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"read\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1792228826293/README.md\\\"}\"}}],\"reasoning\":\"We have a README.md and .gitkeep. Let's check the README to see if there are any instructions.\\n Then we'll create the Scala file and the CI directory.\\n\\n Let's read the README.\",\"reasoning_details\":[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"We have a README.md and .gitkeep. Let's check the README to see if there are any instructions.\\n Then we'll create the Scala file and the CI directory.\\n\\n Let's read the README.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]},{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"call-12a9f39c-e680-4d90-bb32-ae6d07646cf6\",\"content\":\"<file>\\n00001| # hive-mind\\n00002| \\n00003| This is a test repository for automated issue solving.\\n00004| \\n00005| ## Purpose\\n00006| This repository is used to test the `solve.mjs` script that automatically solves GitHub issues.\\n00007| \\n00008| ## Test Issue\\n00009| An issue will be created asking to implement 